[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5523861477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123106#issuecomment-5523861477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123106","id":5523861477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABST9v5Q","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T09:50:03Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T09:50:03Z","body":"> When inspecting a node with an audio bus property and editing audio buses at the same time, it won't automatically refresh the drop-down in the inspector until re-selecting the node. That's pretty much how most dynamic stuff works in Godot so I guess it's working as intended?\r\n\r\nAudioStreamPlayer fixes it by updating property list on bus changes.\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6ef60dc279b2c58a94ffc57bf98eefc9663f7907/scene/audio/audio_stream_player_internal.cpp#L370-L371\r\nFor custom properties, it either needs to be done in the script, or somehow in the created EditorProperty. Although I'd wait until someone reports it as a problem 🤷‍♂️\r\n\r\n> We can discuss what to do if a serialized bus name is no longer found. The current code keeps the old name as is and just selects nothing when opening the drop-down, so in case it gets re-added/renamed, nothing is lost. An alternative would be to force fallback to Master. On the getter side, there is already some logic to fall back to Master if the property points to a non-existing bus.\r\n\r\nReminds me #39605\r\nApparently using non-existent bus name is fine (and makes me think that maybe the bus property should enable loose mode).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5523861477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529823593","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123106#issuecomment-5529823593","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123106","id":5529823593,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSZppaQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T17:51:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T17:51:40Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529823593/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5581757532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123106#issuecomment-5581757532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123106","id":5581757532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTLLcXA","user":{"login":"realkotob","id":43449832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNDQ5ODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43449832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob","html_url":"https://github.com/realkotob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-08T08:25:27Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:25:27Z","body":"> We can discuss what to do if a serialized bus name is no longer found. The current code keeps the old name as is and just selects nothing when opening the drop-down, so in case it gets re-added/renamed, nothing is lost. An alternative would be to force fallback to Master. On the getter side, there is already some logic to fall back to Master if the property points to a non-existing bus.\r\n\r\nI support keeping the current behaviour, I believe that is the best way to handle it. Forcing a default fallback at serialization time can cause a lot of unexpected behaviour and I don't think we should encourage that pattern.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5581757532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]